\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces $N$-independence of the real-space Pfaffian boundary detector versus a conventional spectral-gap threshold detector, at $\mu =0$ (known analytic boundary $B_c=\Delta $). The Pfaffian detector's extracted $B_c$ is exactly $N$-independent (spread $0.0$ across $N=20$--$160$); the threshold detector's extracted $B_c$ drifts by $0.66\,\Delta $ over the same range. Generated by \texttt  {bdg\_r4\_em\_coupling.py}; data in \texttt  {ISEF R4 data folder/}.}}{5}{}}
