\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Validation battery for the physically meaningful coupling regime ($g<g_{\rm  deadzone}$, top of the unambiguous static-boundary regime). (a) $N$-independence of the boundary shift at $g=1\times 10^4$: the shift vanishes as $N\to \infty $ ($\sim N^{-1.8}$ to $N^{-1.9}$). (b) Bisection-tolerance robustness at $g=2\times 10^4$, $N=80$. Generated by \texttt  {bdg\_r5\_physically\_meaningful\_shift.py}; data in \texttt  {ISEF R5 data folder/}.}}{6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:nullvalidation}{{3}{6}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {C}A second observable: the feedback-renormalized reactance}{6}{}}
\newlabel{subsec:impedance}{{III\,C}{6}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The reactive-impedance enhancement $1/(1-s)$ near $g_{\rm  crit}$. (A) On the physical principal branch the enhancement rises smoothly to a bounded maximum ($\sim 5.7\times $ at $N=80$) before the static fixed point detaches via the self-consistency map's sawtooth structure, never reaching a literal $s=1$ divergence. (B) The bounded cap itself grows under mesh refinement at fixed physical length ($\sim 5.6\times $ at $N=80$ to $\sim 9.8\times $ at $N=200$), so a genuine continuum divergence is neither established nor excluded. Generated by \texttt  {bdg\_r9\_pole\_characterization.py}; data in \texttt  {ISEF R8 data folder/}.}}{7}{}}
\newlabel{fig:pole}{{4}{7}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces On-site disorder at $N=80$: (left) fraction of realizations misclassified as topological near a clean-trivial point, growing smoothly and saturating near $30\%$ at the top of the literature-realistic range; (middle) mean spurious sub-gap-state count (flat with $W$) versus its realization-to-realization spread (growing substantially with $W$); (right) mean self-consistent boundary shift versus $W$ at $N=80$ only. \emph  {The right-hand panel predates the finite-size scrutiny described in the text}: a subsequent check at $N=120$ and $N=160$ found the $N=80$ values shown here substantially overstate the effect at the upper end of the disorder range (\S  \ref {subsec:robustness}) -- see Table~\ref {tab:disorderNindep}. Generated by \texttt  {bdg\_r9\_disorder.py}; data in \texttt  {ISEF R9 data folder/}.}}{7}{}}
\newlabel{fig:disorder}{{5}{7}{}{}{}}
