\newlabel{subsec:proxy}{{III\,E}{8}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Single-channel Lutchyn-Oreg $(\mu ,B_{\rm  zeeman})$ phase diagram at realistic InAs/Al parameters: genuine TRIM Pfaffian invariant (left) and ring bulk gap on a log scale (right), analytic boundary overlaid. Idealized/theoretical regime: $\Delta $ is held fixed (no field-dependent pair-breaking), and the plotted Zeeman range exceeds the verified axial critical field of a comparable epitaxial-Al shell by a factor of $\sim 8$ at $\mu =0$~\cite  {chang2015}. Generated by \texttt  {bdg\_r6\_lo\_phase\_diagram.py}; data in \texttt  {R6\_data\_files/}.}}{9}{}}
\newlabel{fig:phasediagram}{{6}{9}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The pre-registered multi-subband loop-gain probe. (A) Truncation convergence at fixed occupancy (a sanity check, not the physics answer): $s$ converges smoothly with basis size. (B) The genuine-occupancy sweep, $s(\mu ;M)$ at production coupling $g=2.9\times 10^4$: the stability boundary $s=1$ is crossed once $M\geq 2$. (C) The pre-registered comparison statistic (median $s$ over the surviving, van-Hove-excluded window): a sharp $M=1\to 2$ jump, then a non-monotonic $M=2\to 3\to 4$ trend. \emph  {This is a structural result at $M\leq 4$, not a device-faithful prediction} -- see text. Generated by \texttt  {bdg\_r9\_multisubband\_sweep.py}; data in \texttt  {ISEF R9 data folder/}.}}{9}{}}
\newlabel{fig:multisubband}{{7}{9}{}{}{}}
