\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces The full self-consistent boundary calculation at one representative $M=2$ operating point ($\mu =131.762$, production coupling $g=2.9\times 10^4$), as a function of system size $N$. A \emph  {genuine}, Anderson-mixing-confirmed root and boundary was found at $N=80$; both neighboring system sizes tested return a robust no-solution (\texttt  {genuine\_dead\_zone}) result across every one of five independently jittered search paths -- the opposite $N$-dependence pattern from the single-channel case, where dead-zones shrink and vanish as $N$ grows. The $N=80$ shift is not quoted as a headline value; see text.}}{10}{}}
\newlabel{tab:m2existence}{{II}{10}{}{}{}}
